y to substations and transformers. Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria, so its increase carries the most weight.\n  - **Financing risk:** Credit conditions tightened a little in Q3 2026. Utility bond spreads widened 30bp to 165bp, and two utility share offerings were cut back in size. Norvane still priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably, so debt funding remains open. The equity pullback could still force some projects to be trimmed or delayed.\n- **Data centres (rising, but slowing):** Grid connection requests from Caldrian data centres are expected to grow 9% in 2027. That is slower than in 2026, because power availability limits new sites. The source gives no 2026 growth rate, so I can't say how much slower. Connection requests are a proxy for equipment demand, not a direct measure of it. The documents also don't say how much of the utility spending is driven by data centres.\n- **Gaps:** I found no data on 2026 spending levels, order backlogs or equipment-maker orders. The utility case rests on two utilities' stated plans.\n\nDetails are in n7.r1 (utilities) and n8.r1 (data centres).","ttft_ms":4919,"type":"result","duration_ms":41287,"uuid":"d29994a5-df10-4b19-982d-fab7ac66383c","ttft_stream_ms":4026,"time_to_request_ms":534,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":65,"system_prompt":38,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":24,"input_attachments":104,"input_hooks":12,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":22,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":49,"init_frame_send":19,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":17,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":18,"request_announcements":55,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":45,"message_normalization":25,"client_creation":30,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":283,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":96,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":186,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":112,"process_rss_mib_resul